segments:
V. 48. Say we not well-Have we not just cause to say, 

  Thou art, a Samaritan-An enemy to our Church and nation; 

  and hast a devil?-Art possessed by a proud and lying spirit?

V. 59. Then they took up stones-To stone him as a blasphemer; 

  but Jesus concealed himself-Probably by becoming invisible; 

  and so passed on-With the same ease as if none had been there.
